  "question": {
    "text": "White light is used to illuminate the two slits in Young's double-slit experiment. The separation between the slits is <math><mi>d</mi></math> and the distance between the slits and screen is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. At a point on the screen directly in front of one of the slits, certain wavelengths are missing. The missing wavelengths are",
